WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.375
Searched CASE is the flexible form of CASE Each WHEN
contains a

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.425
complete Boolean condition so it works well for
ranges compound rules and

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:12.825
NULL checks The billing example handles NULL first
so a missing amount

00:00:12.838 --> 00:00:17.275
is not silently classified as low It then checks the
highest threshold

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.562
followed by the next threshold and uses ELSE for the
remaining known

00:00:20.588 --> 00:00:26.288
values A twelve-thousand-dollar bill matches
High-Value and stops there A

00:00:26.312 --> 00:00:32.162
seventy-five-hundred-dollar bill reaches Standard
Run the example and inspect zero NULL

00:00:32.362 --> 00:00:37.088
and threshold values Searched CASE is especially
useful when the business rule

00:00:37.112 --> 00:00:39.200
itself needs to be visible in the SQL
